1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
A 64 by 64 grayscale image, processed by a microcontroller running in RTL simulation.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,000
The image is read from SPI flash into SRAM. Every byte is checked against the source image.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Two gradient tasks compute the Sobel Gx and Gy for each stripe of four rows.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Combine waits on queues for both gradient stripes. No stripe is combined early.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Combine writes the edge image into the output framebuffer, one stripe at a time.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
The finished frame is read back over UART with a SHA-256 digest.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Baseline result: the stored image matches the OpenCV reference. Zero mismatches.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Fault run: same firmware, same input. The testbench will flip one bit in SRAM.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Fault run: the computation and task schedule replay identically.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:47,000
At the final write of pixel (32, 32), one bit is flipped: 0x00 becomes 0x80.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The corrupted byte is exported over UART. The reference comparison finds exactly one wrong pixel.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The checker rejects the faulty image. Define behavior and verify the evidence.

